A||||5||AkursedX||Where do these wires go??||||1||
Z||000000||AkursedX||07-19-2001||11:48 PM||||Hello.  I have seem to of found some loose wires during my teardown.  <P>They are located along the left side of the engine block, towards the firewall side of the car (v-6)<P>They look like 2 ground wires that should be attached to the firewall side cylinder head.  <P>Does anyone have any idea what I'm talking about?  <P>I will probably have pics of it tomorrow.<P>Thanks in advance for any info  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Joe Torma||07-20-2001||12:11 AM||||Probably grounds that belong on the head...what color are they?<P>Joe||||reg||1
Z||000002||AkursedX||07-20-2001||12:38 AM||||I think they are black and orange, or both black.  I'm thinking the same thing myself, I just want to make sure||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||07-20-2001||01:46 AM||||Don't remember an orange wire, but on my V-6, there were two or three black wires that are grounded to the firewall-side head, just above the tranny.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||07-20-2001||02:52 AM||||AkursedX, that's exactly where they go, left side of the rear of the block under the head......there should be three wires, two mount to one bolt and one to another......holes are provided  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||StuGood||07-20-2001||08:09 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by tgowens:<BR><B>..they go, left side of the rear of the block under the head...two mount to one bolt and one to another......holes are provided   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Think on my 1987 GT, the 2 holes are actually in the <B>head</B> (as opposed to in the block, under the head, as tgowens said).  Picky little twerp, aren't I?  Just trying to clarify.<P>BTW, on mine, I found two ground wires attached to a single lug, which goes under a bolt threaded into the "back" (LHS) of the head.  A third (single) ground wire with a lug, goes under another bolt threaded into  the same end of the same head.<P>Hope this helps.  When it comes to holes in my head, I should know  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   <P>||||reg||1
